                <pb facs="0425" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg425"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Thayer</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 13, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and have read with much
                    interest your despatch of the 29th of June, (No. 3,) announcing your arrival in
                    Egypt, and giving an account of your reception by the viceroy. Your remarks on
                    that occasion, as well as your conduct throughout the imposing ceremonial, are
                    approved, and the friendly feeling towards the United States manifested by his
                    highness in your interview with him, and subsequently by his minister of foreign
                    affairs, and by the consuls general representing other nations in Egypt, is very
                    gratifying.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William S. Thayer</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul General of the United States, Alexandria,
                            Egypt</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
